For a primate with a digestive apparatus similar to that of humans, it is difficult to meet one’s amino acid needs with the plant resources available in the savannah.
In addition, the non-realization of such activities has serious consequences: slowing growth, malnutrition and, in the end, death.
The most easily accessible plant resources would have been the proteins present in leaves and legumes, but for primates like us they are difficult to digest, unless they are cooked.
Animal foods (such as ants, termites, eggs) are not only easy to digest, but provide a high amount of protein, containing all essential amino acids.
In light of all this, it shouldn’t be surprising that our own ancestors solved their “protein problem” in a sense as savannah chimpanzees do today.
Disruption of sleep is the intentional awakening process that occurs during the period of normal sleep, followed by a resumption of sleep (10–60 minutes later).
This process can easily be put into practice using a relatively silent alarm clock to bring you to a state of consciousness, without waking up completely.
If you decide to reset the clock in your sleep, you can put it on the other side of the room, so you’ll have to get out of bed to turn it off.
Other biorhythm-focused options involve consuming plenty of fluids before sleep (mainly water or tea, known for its diuretic properties), which force you to get out of bed to urinate.
A person enjoys an inner peace proportionally opposed to tension existing in his body and spirit.
The less tension, the more positive is the existing life force. Each of us has the potential ability to find absolute peace and fulfillment.
Everyone can achieve enlightenment. This goal is hampered only by our tension and negativity.
Tibetan Buddhism is based on the Buddha's teachings, but it has been enriched by the love path of the Mahayan rite and various techniques of Indian yoga.
In principle, Tibetan Buddhism is very simple. It has foundation in Kundalini Yoga, meditation, and an all-encompassing path of love.
Kundalini Yoga activates Kundalini energy (enlighting energy) through the use of yoga poses, breathing exercises, mantras and visualizations.
Deity Yoga is the fulcrum of Tibetan meditation. Through the depiction of various deities you clean the energetic channels, activate the chakras and develop the consciousness of enlightenment.
Germany was a common enemy in World War II, leading to collaboration between the USSR and the United States. With the end of the war, system conflicts, procedural and cultural, provoked the rupture between the two countries.
After two years after the end of the war, the allies of the past had become enemies; the Cold War began.
It would last for the next 40 years and would have been fought for real, by mercenary armies, in the battlefields from Africa to Asia, Afghanistan, Cuba and many other countries.
On September 17, 1939, the Polish defense had already been broken down; the only option was to beat in retreat and reorganise along the Romanian bridgehead.
However, these plans were immediately obsolete, when more than 800,000 soldiers of the Soviet Red Army advanced and created the Belarusian and Ukrainian fronts, after invading the eastern regions of Poland, violating the Riga peace treaty, the Soviet-Polish non-agggression pact and other international, bilateral and multilateral treaties.
Exploiting ships for the transport of goods is certainly the most efficient way to move large volumes of people and goods across the oceans.
The task of navies has always been the task of guaranteeing the country the protection of its ability to move people and goods, while countering the same ability of enemies to move their people and their goods.
One of the recent examples in support of this theory and most noteworthy is represented by the battle of the Atlantic during World War II. During the battle, the Americans sought to enliven men and goods across the Atlantic Ocean to support Britain.
At the same time the German navy, using mainly submarines, attempted to stop this traffic.
If the Allies had not succeeded, Germany would probably have had a chance to clinch Britain, as it had done in the rest of Europe.
Apparently, the goats were domesticated for the first time about 10,000 years ago in the Zagros Mountains in Iran.
They began to be bred by the cultures and tribes of antiquity to easily have milk, fleece, flesh and skin available.
Domestic goats were usually bred in herds left free to move on the hills or in other grazing areas, often cared for by goats (similar to herders) who were often children or teenagers. These methods of herding are still used nowadays.
Already in the sixteenth century, wagonways were built in England.
Although they were formed simply by parallel wooden axes, the wagonways, when compared to the slightly rougher roads of the period, allowed the horses that traveled them to reach higher speeds and move heavier loads.
The crossbars were introduced relatively soon to keep the tracks in place. Gradually, however, it was understood that the tracks would have been more efficient if they had an iron bar on top.
It became a common practice, even if the iron caused greater wear of the wooden wheels of the wagons.
Finally, the wooden wheels gave way to iron wheels. In 1767, the first all-iron rails appeared.
The first means of transport that man knew were the legs. Humans began to walk upright two million years ago with the appearance of Homo Erectus (meaning "erect man").
His predecessor, the australopithecus, did not routinely walk erect.
Signs of specialization for bipedal gait are present in Australopithecus fossils dating from 4.2-3.9 million years ago, although it's possible that the Sahelanthropus walked on two legs as early as seven million years ago.
To try to mitigate future suffering to some extent we can begin to adopt lifestyles that are more respectful of the environment, we can adhere to the environmental movement and also do activism.
In many cases this only works as a symptomatic treatment. But if we don’t just want a temporary solution, we should find the ultimate cause of the problems and turn it off.
It is quite evident that the world has greatly changed due to the scientific and technological advances of humanity, while the problems have increased due to the overpopulation and extravagant lifestyle of humans.
After Congress adopted it on July 4, a handwritten draft signed by President John Hancock and Secretary Charles Thomson was then sent to John Dunlap's typography a few blocks away.
In the night were produced between 150 and 200 copies, today known as "Dunlap's posters".
The document was read publicly for the first time on July 8 in the Independence Hall's backyard, and John Nixon was commissioned.
One was sent to George Washington on July 6, who had his troops stationed in New York read on 9 July, while a copy arrived in London on August 10.
Dunlap’s 25 broadsides still known are the oldest existing copies of the document. The original manuscript was lost.
According to many paleontologists of today a category of dinosaurs has survived and is still alive. They are what we call birds.
Many tend not to consider them dinosaurs because of the feathers and their ability to fly.
Yet the birds have many characteristics that share them with the dinosaurs.
Like the T-Rex, they come with feet with scales and claws, lay their eggs and walk on their two hind legs.
Ultimately, the manipulation of information encoded in the form of binary numbers is the basis of all currently used computers.
A binary number can only have one of two values, i.e. 0 or 1, and in the computer technical language these numbers are called binary digits or bits.
The internal poisoning may not be immediately noticeable. Its symptoms, including vomiting, are very generic, so as to make an immediate diagnosis impossible.
The main indication of internal poisoning could be the presence in the home of a container of drugs or open harmful chemicals.
Check if there are first aid instructions on the label for that specific poison.
The term mite is formally used by entomologists for this insect group.
The term comes from familiarity in ancient times with bed bugs, insects that have strongly adapted to becoming human parasites.
Both killer bugs and bed bugs are nesty, i.e. adapted to live in the nest or home of their guest.
In the United States, multiple sclerosis (MS) recorded about 400,000 known cases, ranking first among neurological diseases that affect young people and middle-aged adults.
MS is a pathology that affects the central nervous system, which includes the brain, spinal cord and optic nerve.
Research has shown that the chances of developing MS among females are dual compared to males.
A couple can decide that raising a child is not in their interest, or that of their child.
These couples have the option of choosing an adoption plan for their child.
In an adoption, natural parents waive their parental rights so that another couple can raise the child.
The primary objective of science is to understand the way the world works through the scientific method. This method effectively guides most of the scientific investigation.
But it's not just about experimentation, since an experiment is a test used to rule out one or more of the possible hypotheses; even asking questions and making observations allows you to orient scientific research.
Naturalists and philosophers focused on classical texts, especially the Latin version of the Bible.
Aristotle’s views on the various subjects of knowledge, including psychology, were accepted.
With the progressive decline of the Greek language, the West has been isolated from its Greek philosophical and scientific roots.
Many have observed that physiological rhythms and behavior depend decisively on the presence of endogenous cycles and their production through biological clocks.
Periodic rhythms have been documented, which are not only reactions to external periodic signals, relative to most living things, including bacteria, fungi, plants and animals.
Biological clocks are independent oscillators, whose free cycle continues for a period of time even in the absence of external stimuli.
One of the first experiments to suggest that DNA was a genetic material was the one conducted by Hershey and Chase.
Hershey and Chase used bacteriophages, i.e. viruses, to implant their own DNA into a bacterium.
They performed two experiments by highlightinging bacteriophage DNA with radioactive phosphorus or bacteriophagus protein with radioactive sulfur.
Mutations can have a number of different effects based on the type of mutation, the relevance of the piece of genetic material involved, and depending on whether the affected cells belong to the germinal line.
Mutations that can be transmitted to children are only those at the level of germ cells; mutations that occur elsewhere can cause cell death or cancer.
Naturistic tourism attracts people interested in visiting natural areas with the aim of enjoying the landscape, including flora and wildlife.
Among the examples of activities to do on the spot are hunting, fishing, photography, birdwatching, visits to parks and the study of information regarding the ecosystem.
For example, by visiting, photographing and learning about Borneo’s orangutans.
Every morning, people quit small country towns to drive to work, crossing other people whose workplace is the place from which they have just departed.
In this dynamic coming and going, everyone is somehow connected to a transport system based on private cars, which at the same time support.
Today science reveals that this massive carbon-based economy has forced the biosphere outside one of its stability conditions that has enabled human evolution over the last two million years.
Every person participates in social life and uses transport systems, of which almost everyone complains.
In developed countries it is rare to hear similar levels of comprisons concerning water quality or bridges falling into disrepair.
Why do transport systems attract so many complaints, why are they rejected every day? Are the engineers who design them who are incompetent, or are there deeper motivations?
"Traffic Flow" (i.e
Unfortunately, the study of traffic flow is complex since the behavior of drivers cannot be predicted with absolute certainty.
Luckily, the behavior of drivers tends to fall within a reasonably constant range, so, in turn, traffic flows tend to show reasonable consistency and can be represented generically mathematically.
To obtain a more accurate representation of the traffic flow, the three main variables were correlated: (1) range, (2) density and (3) velocity.
These reports are useful for planning, designing, and managing road structures.
Insects were the first animals to take flight. The ability to fly allowed them to escape the enemies more easily and to find food and companions more efficiently.
Most insects are advantaged by the ability to fold their wings along the body.
This allows them to take advantage of a greater variety of small ravines for hiding from predators.
Among all existing insects nowadays, the only ones that are unable to fold the wings are dragonflies and ephemerals.
Thousands of years ago, a man called Aristarchus claimed that the solar system was moving around the Sun.
For some he was right, but many others believed the opposite, namely that the solar system, including the Sun itself (and the other stars), moved around the Earth.
Which seems sensible, because we don't have a feeling that the Earth is moving, right?
The Amazon River is the largest river and the longest on Earth. It carries an amount of water equal to 8 times that of the second largest river.
The Amazon River is also Earth's widest river, with a width that in some places reaches six miles.
The total 20% of the water pouring from the planet's rivers into the oceans comes from the Amazon River.
The Main Amazon River is 6,387 km (3,980 miles) long. In it the waters of thousands of minor tributaries pour.
Pyramids continued in stone until the end of the Old Kingdom, but despite this the pyramids of Giza were never surpassed in terms of grandeur and technical excellence of their realization.
The ancient Egyptians of the New Reign remained enchanting admiring the monuments of their ancestors, who at that time were much more than a thousand years old.
The population of the Vatican City consists of about 800 inhabitants. It is the smallest independent state in the world and the one with the least population.
The language of Vatican City for official legislation and communications is Italian.
Italian is also the language of daily use spoken by most people working within the state, while Latin is often used in religious services.
In Vatican City, all citizens are Roman Catholics.
Man has begun to know the basic chemical elements such as gold, silver and copper already in antiquity: these elements can be discovered in nature in native form and it is possible to extract them quite simply with the help of primitive tools.
According to the Philosopher Aristotle, everything is composed of a combination of one or more of the following four elements: earth, water, air and fire.
These in fact look more like the four states of matter, i.e. (in the same order): solid, liquid, gaseous and plasma. However, he also theorized that they were transformed into new substances, forming what we see.
Alloys are basically a mixture of two or more metals. Keep in mind that the periodical table contains numerous elements.
Elements like calcium and potassium are believed to be metals. Obviously, metals such as silver and gold also exist.
There can also be alloys made up of minimal amounts of non-metallic elements, such as carbon.
In the universe, everything is made of matter and all matter consists of tiny particles called atoms.
Atoms are incredibly tiny, so much so that trillions of them could get into the spot at the end of this sentence.
