Christmas is one of the most important festivals of Christianity and celebrates the birth of Jesus.
Much of the traditions related to this festivity have also been adopted by non-believers in Christian countries and by non-Christians around the world.
A tradition involves spending the night of Easter staying awake in an outdoor place in order to admire the sunrise.
Of course, there are Christian theological explanations underlying this tradition, but it could very well be a pre-crystistian ritual related to spring and fertility.
