In Japan, the culture of work is more hierarchical and formal than that to which Westerners tend to be accustomed.
Office clothing is normally made up of jacket and tie or suit and you turn to your colleagues with your surname or professional title.
The harmony of the workplace is of crucial importance, since it gives importance to the commitment of the group rather than commendating individual achievements.
